- `/Users/michael/Code/cipher-box/tests/web-e2e/tests/streaming-playback.spec.ts` (lines 50-55, 116-121)

**Issue:** All three test suites upload multiple files in sequential loops with full waits between uploads:
```typescript
for (const file of [file1, file2, file3]) {
  await uploadZone.uploadFile(file.path);
  await uploadZone.waitForUploadComplete({ timeout: 30_000 }); // Blocks next file
  await fileList.waitForItemToAppear(file.name, { timeout: 30_000 });
}
```

This unnecessarily blocks upload N+1 until upload N completes. If the system supports concurrent uploads, this is a bottleneck.

**Suggestion:** Start all uploads, then wait for all completions in parallel:
```typescript
// Start all uploads
const uploadPromises = [file1, file2, file3].map(file => 
  uploadZone.uploadFile(file.path)
);
await Promise.all(uploadPromises);

// Wait for all to appear
await Promise.all([
  fileList.waitForItemToAppear(file1Name, { timeout: 30_000 }),
  fileList.waitForItemToAppear(file2Name, { timeout: 30_000 }),
  fileList.waitForItemToAppear(file3Name, { timeout: 30_000 }),
]);
```

